{%- comment -%}
	Numbered steps — a short ordered list for text that tells someone what to
	do, or what happens next. The numerals match the affiliate agreement's card
	headings: heading face, highlight colour, "1." The caller sets the text
	classes, so the list can sit on a white card or on the hero photo.

	Parameters:
	  steps        {Array}   the step texts, in order (required)
	  list_class   {String}  layout classes for the list   (default: stacked, 'flex flex-col gap-3')
	  text_class   {String}  classes for each step's text  (default: 'text-base text-title')
	  number_class {String}  size classes for the numerals (default: 'text-xl')

	Usage:
	  {%- assign steps = 'First%%Second' | split: '%%' -%}
	  {%- render 'numbered-steps', steps: steps -%}
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
	assign steps_list_class = list_class | default: 'flex flex-col gap-3'
	assign steps_text_class = text_class | default: 'text-base text-title'
	assign steps_number_class = number_class | default: 'text-xl'
-%}

{%- comment -%} role="list": Safari drops list semantics from a list with no markers. The numeral is decoration, the position is announced by the list. {%- endcomment -%}
<ol role="list" class="list-none p-0 m-0 {{ steps_list_class }}">
	{%- for step in steps -%}
		<li class="flex items-baseline gap-1.5">
			{%- comment -%} A fixed width, in the numeral's own size, so every step's text starts on the same line whatever the digit. {%- endcomment -%}
			<span class="font-heading heading-weight text-highlight shrink-0 w-[1.3em] {{ steps_number_class }}" aria-hidden="true">{{ forloop.index }}.</span>
			<span class="{{ steps_text_class }}">{{ step }}</span>
		</li>
	{%- endfor -%}
</ol>
